WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:09.000
<v Yara Kamal>Thanks both for joining. We are going rider by rider through this month's feedback calls, so I will write up the themes after.

2
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:15.000
<v Pieter Bos>Happy to start. The first rider this morning was a commuter in Utrecht who rides every day, and the first thing she said was the motor is so quiet.

3
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:21.000
<v Yara Kamal>That is the praise we hear most. Did she say anything about the assist feel itself?

4
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:27.000
<v Pieter Bos>She said the power comes in smoothly from a standstill, and she does not get the whine she had on her old bike.

5
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:32.000
<v Greta Fuchs>My calls were mostly from Berlin. The quiet motor came up in four of the six, usually without any prompting.

6
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:38.000
<v Yara Kamal>Good. Now the complaints. Greta, what came up on app pairing?

7
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:46.000
<v Greta Fuchs>Three riders could not pair a new phone with the bike. Two had pairing work on the first try and then lost it after a phone update.

8
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:52.000
<v Yara Kamal>Did any of them already have the latest app version installed when it failed?

9
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:58.000
<v Greta Fuchs>Yes, two of the three. So it is not only old app versions. That is worth telling Engineering directly.

10
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:04.000
<v Pieter Bos>On my side, the calls in Dutch were mostly about winter. Riders say the range shown on the screen drops quickly once the temperature falls.

11
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:10.000
<v Yara Kamal>Slow winter range is the complaint I expected. Did anyone ask whether the display is wrong, or whether the bike is wrong?

12
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:17.000
<v Pieter Bos>Most asked whether the bike is wrong. I told them the cold reduces what the battery can deliver, and I did not promise a fix.

13
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:22.000
<v Greta Fuchs>A rider in Hamburg wanted a comparison with the old model. She was happy with the answer once she saw the numbers.

14
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:28.000
<v Yara Kamal>Good. Let us keep that answer in the shared script. Anything else that repeats across the calls?

15
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:35.000
<v Pieter Bos>Two riders asked for a longer warranty on the saddle and the grips. I said I would pass it on and did not commit to anything.

16
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:41.000
<v Yara Kamal>Thanks. I will write up the three themes this afternoon: quiet motor, app pairing, winter range. Pieter, send the Dutch examples to me with the escalation.
